  "question": {
    "text": "Let $z$ be a complex number such that $|z+2|=1$ and $\\operatorname{Im}\\left(\\frac{z+1}{z+2}\\right)=\\frac{1}{5}$. Then the value of $|\\operatorname{Re}(\\overline{z+2})|$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{2 \\sqrt{6}}{5}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{24}{5}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{1+\\sqrt{6}}{5}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{5}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$|z+2|=1, \\operatorname{Im}\\left(\\frac{z+1}{z+2}\\right)=\\frac{1}{5}$<br />Let $z+2=\\cos \\theta+i \\sin \\theta$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{1}{z+2}=\\cos \\theta-i \\sin \\theta \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\frac{z+1}{z+2}=1-\\frac{1}{z+2}=1-(\\cos \\theta-i \\sin \\theta) \\\\\n& =(1-\\cos \\theta)+\\operatorname{isin} \\theta \\\\\n& \\operatorname{Im}\\left(\\frac{z+1}{z+2}\\right)=\\sin \\theta, \\sin \\theta=\\frac{1}{5} \\\\\n& \\cos \\theta= \\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{1}{25}}= \\pm \\frac{2 \\sqrt{6}}{5} \\\\\n& |\\operatorname{Re}(\\overline{z+2})|=\\frac{2 \\sqrt{6}}{5}\n\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}